title One prover for twenty-seven
prompt Keaton: grant all your best recommendations.
rota none -- a granted queue rather than a rota row; the Aether row was read at 20260907.234808 and Water's seat changed at 20260908.001350.
think A blanket grant is the moment to be narrower rather than wider, so I took the recommendations I had actually named and started with the one blocking the fleet.
think It was already gone. The ledger deadlock I left red an hour ago now reads verdict=ok: a peer reached the same conclusion in the same hour and moved the teeth to the instrument that holds the remote, leaving the count where it is cheap. My recommendation was right and somebody else took it, which is what eight ships on one tree is for.
obs SO THE GRANT POINTED AT THE 27 UNPROVEN WRITERS, AND THE OBVIOUS REPAIR WAS THE CENSUS'S OWN FINDING REPEATED. Hand-writing a convergence case into each of 27 controls is exactly a rule kept where a hand remembered -- performed 27 times. 22 of the 27 share one invocation shape, a single file path, so one prover answers for all of them and the five that differ are named rather than skipped in silence.
obs THE THIRD VERDICT IS THE ONE THAT EARNS THE TOOL. `inert` says the FIRST run changed nothing, so the sample exercised no path and the reading proves nothing. A sample that triggers no work is the quiet way a convergence proof lies -- it returns green having tested the absence of work. The control plants exactly that case and requires it to be named rather than counted as a pass.
obs I WROTE AN ASSERTION THAT WOULD HAVE PASSED ONLY WHEN THE THING IT GUARDS WAS BROKEN. The witness asserted on a check's message text -- and `check` prints only on FAILURE, so the assertion was satisfied exactly when the control failed. It caught itself immediately because the control was passing. The control now says its coverage out loud, which is the honest fix: a witness should assert on a statement of what happened, never on the wording of a complaint.
obs AND THE FIRST REAL WRITER TESTED CONVERGES. ascii_document_convert, run twice on an em dash and an ellipsis, leaves the file byte-identical after the second run. The property was true all along and unproven -- which is what the census measured and what this prover now closes, one tool at a time, without hand-writing 27 of anything.
loom convergence_prove control_pass=12 control_fail=0 diverging_tool_caught=yes inert_named=yes
loom convergence_shape unproven=27 share_one_file_arg=22 differ=5
loom convergence_first_proof tool=ascii_document_convert verdict=converges sample_inert=no
file tools/c/convergence_prove.sh the prover -- two runs on a copy, three verdicts, the tree never touched
file tools/fixtures/c/convergence_prove_control.sh twelve behaviors, including a tool built to diverge and a sample built to prove nothing
file tools/c/convergence_prove_witness.rish the guard, rostered tier lap
scope one granted queue -- the blocking red found already closed by a peer, and the next recommendation built as a loom rather than 27 repetitions
status GREEN -- control 12 of 12, witness green, roster pass ok, tracked links ok; the ledger deadlock reads verdict=ok on the peer's repair
recommend keep-going -- run the prover across the 22 sharing the file shape and record which converge, then name the 5 that differ; that is a measurement rather than a build.
